---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About AstroPublishKit and this public demo site.">
  <article class="shell prose standalone-prose">
    <h1>About AstroPublishKit</h1>
    <p>
      AstroPublishKit is a static-first publishing foundation for blogs, technical notes, and
      content-focused sites. This site is the public reference deployment of the starter.
    </p>
    <h2>What belongs in the kit</h2>
    <p>
      Typed content, discoverability, static search, quality checks, and deployment defaults belong
      here. Your brand, editorial voice, analytics accounts, and production content do not.
    </p>
    <h2>Where to customize</h2>
    <p>
      Start with <code>astro-publish-kit.config.mjs</code>, then adjust
      <code>src/styles/global.css</code> if you want a different visual system. Optional integrations
      stay disabled until you provide their environment variables.
    </p>
    <h2>Source code</h2>
    <p>
      The project is MIT licensed and maintained on
      <a href="https://github.com/oyjq0000/AstroPublishKit">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
